{
  "configuration_id": "config_030",
  "reason": "The single completed experiment (config_026, multimodal singleprofile scvi_n200+resnet50 weighted) achieved ~54% accuracy, providing only a weak baseline. The most impactful untested design choice is whether multiprofile aggregation improves over singleprofile, as it fundamentally changes how cellular information is integrated. config_030 isolates this variable: it keeps the same RNA encoder (scvi_n200), image encoder (resnet50), and fusion strategy (weighted) as the baseline, changing only singleprofile→multiprofile with avgpool aggregation. This is a controlled, informative test: if multiprofile+avgpool improves accuracy, it justifies further investment in stronger aggregators (transformer); if not, it confirms singleprofile suffices and saves GPU hours. Expected relative cost is moderate—roughly 1.5–2× the 0.59 GPU hours of the baseline (≈0.9–1.2 GPU hours) due to processing multiple profiles and the avgpool step, but well below transformer-aggregation variants. This is the best use of experiment 2 because it reduces the largest architectural uncertainty at a controlled cost, preserving budget for follow-up exploitation in the remaining 7 experiments."
}

